=== 2026-10-29 alignment with the runtime evidence formats (coordinator edit) ===
Reason: the runtime side (vision_run.MirrorCapture) writes tcpdump statistics into mirror_capture.json['tcpdump'] and
the interface identity as parsed ethtool -i plus ip -j -s link output; campaign_base takes the switch counter
snapshots before and after the whole Vision step, so the counters can include relay-leg frames outside the mirror
capture window. Changes: readers use the runtime formats; copies-vs-counter checks are bounds (copies <= counter),
while dev10 TX == dev64 RX + TX, connection copies == master-NIC frames (off arm), tcpdump captured == records,
zero drops and no truncation stay exact gates. New test: a wider counter window passes with uncaptured reported, and
more copies than counted fails. Order note: the code change was made before the new test was written (not RED first).

=== 2026-10-29 fixes from the independent code review (coordinator edit) ===
HIGH: E2 classified "no egress copy" before checking the ingress copies, so a capture-missed copy that the relay
answered was placed "before or inside the switch". Fix: that contradiction goes to the existing UNCLASSIFIED class;
E2 is usable only when D3a, D3b, D3c and completeness of every E2-block trial pass (D3c_e2_block).
MEDIUM: removed the false assumption that the capture brackets the snapshots; copies <= capture-interface RX packets
is now a gated bound; NIC rx drop/miss/discard/error counter deltas are reported; D3a also requires the registered
bus-info 0000:3b:00.1 (LOW).
New tests (4) written after the code change; mutation check: with the UNCLASSIFIED line removed the contradiction
test FAILS (1 failed), restored file -> 29 passed.
